* Civilian records: DBSITMS-IA-SAR@mod.gov.uk<mailto:DBSITMS-IA-SAR@mod.gov.uk>

If you want a reference
Please note that we are not a point of contact for employee references – instead, these should be directed to peopleservices@dbs.mod.uk<mailto:peopleservices@dbs.mod.uk> or the relevant MOD Force.

If you are an Afghan seeking assistance
Please get in touch with the UK Foreign and Commonwealth office, Consular Services Special Afghanistan Team on 02475 389980, or email crisis@fcdo.org.uk or help@fcdo.gov.uk<mailto:help@fcdo.gov.uk>. The Afghan Relocations and Assistance Policy (ARAP) closed to new applications on 1 July 2025. Applications received before that date will continue to be processed, and applicants can continue to check the progress of their application with the ARAP Eligibility Self-Checker<https://www.gov.uk/government/publications/afghan-relocations-and-assistance-policy/implementation-of-the-online-arap-eligibility-self-checker-for-applicants-beta> tool. For tracking progress on approved ARAP applications please contact: ARAP-Casework@mod.gov.uk<mailto:ARAP-Casework@mod.gov.uk>

